Path operations are evaluated in order [1]. If `/users/{user_id}` is declared before `/users/me`, it will match the request for `/users/me` first and treat `"me"` as the value for `user_id` [1]. To fix this, you must declare the path for `/users/me` before the one for `/users/{user_id}` [1]:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/users/me")
async def read_user_me():
    return {"user_id": "the current user"}

@app.get("/users/{user_id}")
async def read_user(user_id: str):
    return {"user_id": user_id}
```
